[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Note on E8 and E29 (uncomparable UB)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m These two rows are the only rejections whose C behaviour is a **process crash**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m rather than a return value:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - E8: `classify_mode(NULL)` → `strcmp` dereferences a null pointer.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - E29: verified empirically with a `dlopen` probe against the real C `.so`:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `modeselect(-1, 0, 0, 0)` terminates the process with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `Segmentation fault (core dumped)` (exit 139).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m A differential test cannot assert "both returned the same error code" when one
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m side has no return value at all, and deliberately making the Rust crash would
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m make the library strictly worse without making it more faithful. Both rows are
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m therefore recorded as documented-and-excluded rather than asserted, and the tests
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `e8_classify_mode_null_is_documented_ub` and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `e29_modeselect_negative_selector_segfaults_in_c` encode that reasoning (the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m latter proves the C crashes by running the call in a forked child and checking
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m for `SIGSEGV`, and proves the Rust does not crash).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m For E29 the Rust substitutes an empty mode string, which routes to the same
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `classify_mode` result of `0x00` the crash-free portion of the C would have
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m produced. Every non-crashing `mode_selector` (all `>= 0`, plus negative
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m multiples of 4 including `INT_MIN`) is covered by asserted differential rows.
